---
title: "Quick Access Toolbar"
enterprise: true
---

The Toolbar appears above the grid and provides quick access to common grid actions. It supports built-in items, custom components, and configurable ordering and alignment.

Configure the Toolbar with the `toolbar` grid option. The property takes a list of Toolbar Items.

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    toolbar: {
        items: ['columnChooser', 'csvExport', 'resetColumns']
    }
}
```

{% gridExampleRunner title="Built-in Items" name="built-in-items" /%}

## Built-in Items

The following built-in items are available as string shorthands:

-   `columnChooser`: Opens the Column Chooser dialog.
-   `csvExport`: Exports grid data as CSV.
-   `resetColumns`: Resets all columns to their default state.

Built-in items require their corresponding modules to be registered. For example, `columnChooser` requires the `ColumnMenuModule` and `csvExport` requires the `CsvExportModule`. If a required module is not registered, the item will not render and a console warning will be logged.

## Configuration

Items are rendered in the order they are defined.

The `alignment` property can be `left` (default) or `right`.

The `key` uniquely identifies a Toolbar Item.

Additional props are passed to Toolbar Items using `toolbarItemParams`.

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    toolbar: {
        items: [
            'columnChooser',
            {
                key: 'myItem',
                component: CustomToolbarComponent,
                alignment: 'right',
                toolbarItemParams: {
                    label: 'Custom Label'
                }
            }
        ]
    }
}
```

### Display Mode

Items can be displayed as icons only (default) or icons with labels. Set the `display` property at the toolbar level or per item. Item-level settings take precedence.

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    toolbar: {
        display: 'iconAndLabel',
        items: [
            'columnChooser',
            { component: 'csvExport', display: 'icon' }
        ]
    }
}
```

## Custom Components

Custom Toolbar Item components implement the `IToolbarItemComp` interface.

